{
  "_comment": [
    "WATANI GRP Water Tank -- STEEL ACCESSORIES diagram layout spec.",
    "",
    "This file is the DEFAULT (shipped) definition of the reinforcing reference",
    "drawings: for each tank height grade, WHERE each steel member sits on a",
    "side/partition panel elevation. steel_accessories.js renders it to SVG and",
    "binds every member to (a) a PART MASTER DB part number and (b) the formula",
    "row that produces its quantity (AccessoriesRules.reinforcing.<ruleSet>.rows).",
    "",
    "IT DOES NOT AFFECT ANY BOM QUANTITY. Quantities always come from",
    "AccessoriesEngine.reinforcingRowDetail(); this file only decides what is",
    "drawn and what each drawn element points at.",
    "",
    "COORDINATES are in METRES on the panel elevation, origin = bottom-left of",
    "the panel block. x runs 0..cols (cols = the drawing's reference panel count,",
    "NOT the tank's real width -- these sheets are standard-arrangement",
    "references, exactly like the original Excel drawings). y runs 0..H_O.",
    "Any x/y/length field may be a number OR a formula string evaluated by",
    "rule_engine.js with { H_O, H_C, H_F } in scope, e.g. \"H_O-1\".",
    "",
    "geom.kind:",
    "  h      horizontal bar   { y, x1, x2 }",
    "  v      vertical bar     { x, y1, y2 }",
    "  rect   frame / bracket  { x1, x2, y, h, open?: 'bottom'|'top'|'none' }",
    "  marker bracket node     { xs: [..], yFrom, yStep, yTo }  (yTo may be a formula)",
    "",
    "BINDING:",
    "  rowId  -> AccessoriesRules.reinforcing.<ruleSet>.rows[].id (the formula).",
    "            Leave null when the drawing shows a part that has no formula row;",
    "            the audit panel then reports it as an unbound member.",
    "  partNo -> parts_db.json partNo. Leave null to auto-resolve from the row's",
    "            partNumbers entry (this is REQUIRED for SA2/SA4 material-prefix",
    "            parts so the bolt-spec choice keeps deciding the suffix).",
    "  aliasLabel -> the label as printed on the original Excel drawing, kept for",
    "            traceability where it differs from the DB part number",
    "            (e.g. drawing 'WBR-1780Z' is DB 'WCP-1780Z').",
    "",
    "Positions in this first release were transcribed from the original drawing",
    "sheets and cross-checked against each row's formula (a member is listed for",
    "exactly the heights where its formula is non-zero). Fine positioning can be",
    "adjusted in the app's '도면 편집' mode and re-exported over this file."
  ],
